523
00:20:32,540 --> 00:20:34,660
 And the reason why, the reason why you should listen

524
00:20:34,660 --> 00:20:37,420
 to someone like that, both a girl, but also a man,

525
00:20:37,420 --> 00:20:42,140
 is because a person like that is not someone

526
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:44,660
 that you're choosing to follow them.

527
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:47,900
 You're choosing to follow the Jesus that they are following.

528
00:20:47,900 --> 00:20:48,860
 That's what Paul gets at.

529
00:20:48,860 --> 00:20:50,300
 He's like, "Hey, follow me as I follow Christ.

530
00:20:50,300 --> 00:20:51,300
 "What's the implication there?

531
00:20:51,300 --> 00:20:52,300
 "You're not really following me.

532
00:20:52,300 --> 00:20:54,340
 "We're all following the same God.

533
00:20:54,340 --> 00:20:55,420
 "We're following Jesus.

534
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:58,020
 "And so you are not choosing to follow him

535
00:20:58,020 --> 00:20:59,620
 "as much as you're recognizing

536
00:20:59,620 --> 00:21:01,340
 "that he has chosen to follow Christ."

537
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:03,620
 That's what you're doing in that moment.

538
00:21:03,620 --> 00:21:05,740
 Esther trusts Mordecai.

539
00:21:05,740 --> 00:21:07,620
 We should do so similar.

540
00:21:07,620 --> 00:21:09,420
 Here's the thing.

541
00:21:09,420 --> 00:21:12,720
 When you don't do this, when you get offended

542
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:15,220
 because it was a man's idea and it wasn't a woman's idea,

543
00:21:15,220 --> 00:21:17,300
 or you read into his words

544
00:21:17,300 --> 00:21:19,660
 and you negatively interpret everything that he said,

545
00:21:19,660 --> 00:21:21,380
 even things that he didn't say,

546
00:21:21,380 --> 00:21:23,640
 but now he's wondering if he did actually say,

547
00:21:23,640 --> 00:21:25,860
 or you assume the worst rather than assuming the best,

548
00:21:25,860 --> 00:21:28,780
 it perpetuates this false idea that all men

549
00:21:28,780 --> 00:21:29,940
 are not to be trusted.

550
00:21:29,940 --> 00:21:32,220
 Let me be very clear.

551
00:21:32,220 --> 00:21:34,440
 Some men are not to be trusted.

552
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:38,380
 But some men are.

553
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:43,380
 And it's because they know God and they know his word

554
00:21:43,380 --> 00:21:46,580
 and they conform their life to that of Christ's.

555
00:21:46,580 --> 00:21:50,940
 And what you're trusting is not them, but Christ in them.

556
00:21:50,940 --> 00:21:52,100
 That make sense?

557
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:53,160
 It's important.

558
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:55,860
 We should have this sort of approach to each other.

559
00:21:55,860 --> 00:21:59,820
 Paul says, follow me as I follow Christ.

560
00:21:59,820 --> 00:22:03,420
 Ladies, he was a godly man and a similar dignity

561
00:22:03,420 --> 00:22:04,780
 can be offered to your brothers

562
00:22:04,780 --> 00:22:08,500
 if they are demonstrating an equal kind of godliness.

563
00:22:08,500 --> 00:22:10,420
 Godly men care about godly women.

564
00:22:10,420 --> 00:22:12,700
 Godly women trust godly men.

565
00:22:12,700 --> 00:22:15,360
 We have different roles and we have the same value.

566
00:22:15,360 --> 00:22:16,460
 And we recognize that value

567
00:22:16,460 --> 00:22:17,980
 because Christ recognized that value.

568
00:22:17,980 --> 00:22:21,800
 Christ, he moved into our story doing whatever it took

569
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:24,720
 in order to dignify our value

570
00:22:24,720 --> 00:22:26,460
 in a way that both of us have.

571
00:22:26,460 --> 00:22:29,980
 He demonstrated care in a paternal way

572
00:22:29,980 --> 00:22:33,420
 and he demonstrated trust in a maternal way.

573
00:22:33,420 --> 00:22:36,580
 He trusted the father and he cared for his people

574
00:22:36,580 --> 00:22:38,420
 and we should do so similarly.

575
00:22:38,420 --> 00:22:39,820
 But it's not just that.

576
00:22:39,820 --> 00:22:42,300
 As we keep reading in the story of Esther and Mordecai,

577
00:22:42,300 --> 00:22:44,900
 we learn that we have different strengths,

578
00:22:44,900 --> 00:22:46,580
 but we have the same courage.

579
00:22:46,580 --> 00:22:49,700
 We have different strengths, but we have the same courage.

580
00:22:49,700 --> 00:22:51,660
 As you turn the page into chapter three,

581
00:22:51,660 --> 00:22:53,220
 we're introduced to the villain of the story.

582
00:22:53,220 --> 00:22:55,220
 We're introduced to Haman.

583
00:22:55,220 --> 00:22:58,460
 The text tells us that he is an Agagite,

584
00:22:58,460 --> 00:23:00,460
 which just means that he is descendant

585
00:23:00,460 --> 00:23:04,100
 of a guy named Agon who is of the Amalekites.

586
00:23:04,100 --> 00:23:05,580
 If you've read the Old Testament,

587
00:23:05,580 --> 00:23:07,320
 if you're familiar with Christian history,

588
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:09,180
 then what you know is the Amalekites

589
00:23:09,180 --> 00:23:11,620
 were this vicious, bloodthirsty sort of people.

590
00:23:11,620 --> 00:23:14,820
 They were opponents to the people of God.

591
00:23:14,820 --> 00:23:16,580
 And so what we know is that Haman,

592
00:23:16,580 --> 00:23:17,740
 who is actually by this point,

593
00:23:17,740 --> 00:23:19,700
 he's second in command to King Xerxes.

594
00:23:19,700 --> 00:23:22,060
 He's CFO of all Persia.

595
00:23:22,060 --> 00:23:24,620
 We know that this is a very entitled,

596
00:23:24,620 --> 00:23:26,580
 a similarly narcissistic,

597
00:23:26,580 --> 00:23:30,180
 and a win-at-all-costs type of person.

598
00:23:30,180 --> 00:23:34,300
 And then we read that Mordecai responds to him like this.

599
00:23:34,300 --> 00:23:36,400
 It says this in chapter three, verse one.

600
00:23:36,400 --> 00:23:42,660
 After these things, King Ahasuerus, which is King Xerxes,

601
00:23:42,660 --> 00:23:47,300
 he promoted Haman the Agagite, the son of Hamadatha,

602
00:23:47,300 --> 00:23:49,060
 and advanced him and set his throne

603
00:23:49,060 --> 00:23:50,900
 of all the officials who were with him.

604
00:23:50,900 --> 00:23:52,700
 And all the king's servants who were at the king's gate,

605
00:23:52,700 --> 00:23:55,100
 they bowed down and they paid homage to Haman,

606
00:23:55,100 --> 00:23:57,300
 but the king had so commanded concerning him.

607
00:23:57,300 --> 00:24:00,780
 But Mordecai did not bow down or pay homage.

608
00:24:00,780 --> 00:24:01,620
 Why?

609
00:24:01,620 --> 00:24:04,420
 Why doesn't Mordecai bow to Haman?

610
00:24:04,420 --> 00:24:08,060
 The reason why is because in Persian culture,

611
00:24:08,060 --> 00:24:12,540
 kings were esteemed as having a divine sort of essence.

612
00:24:12,540 --> 00:24:16,860
 And so you would bow not to respect them as king,

613
00:24:16,860 --> 00:24:18,900
 but to worship them as king.

614
00:24:18,900 --> 00:24:21,380
 And anyone that they commissioned to be bowed down to

615
00:24:21,380 --> 00:24:23,400
 as well was being offered the same sort

616
00:24:23,400 --> 00:24:25,220
 of divine acknowledgement.

617
00:24:25,220 --> 00:24:27,980
 And so Haman is saying, I'm not bowing to you

618
00:24:27,980 --> 00:24:30,900
 because I can't give to man what is only due to God.

619
00:24:30,900 --> 00:24:35,220
 I do not worship man, I worship the living God.

620
00:24:35,220 --> 00:24:36,940
 Which tells us something really important

621
00:24:36,940 --> 00:24:38,420
 about masculine courage.

622
00:24:38,420 --> 00:24:41,520
 It tells us that courage comes from conviction, gentlemen.

623
00:24:41,520 --> 00:24:44,860
 Your courage, it comes from conviction.

624
00:24:44,860 --> 00:24:47,060
 To be clear, ladies, you have courage

625
00:24:47,060 --> 00:24:48,420
 that comes from conviction also.

626
00:24:48,420 --> 00:24:51,740
 But in this moment, and particularly within the male subset,

627
00:24:51,740 --> 00:24:53,980
 there's maybe a natural orientation

628
00:24:53,980 --> 00:24:57,120
 in the direction of conviction that evokes courage.

629
00:24:57,120 --> 00:25:00,860
 So as an example, in AD 155, brief history less than,

630
00:25:00,860 --> 00:25:03,620
 Polycarp, who is an elderly Christian bishop,

631
00:25:03,620 --> 00:25:05,940
 was arrested by Roman soldiers due to his allegiance

632
00:25:05,940 --> 00:25:07,500
 to Jesus.

633
00:25:07,500 --> 00:25:10,260
 Upon their arrival, these Roman soldiers,

634
00:25:10,260 --> 00:25:11,820
 Polycarp did not flee,

635
00:25:11,820 --> 00:25:14,780
 but instead he invited them into his home.

636
00:25:14,780 --> 00:25:19,500
 And he asked, commanded his companions to get food

637
00:25:19,500 --> 00:25:21,580
 and water for them, that they might be refreshed

638
00:25:21,580 --> 00:25:23,420
 as he prayed before they left.

639
00:25:23,420 --> 00:25:24,240
 Left to where?

640
00:25:24,240 --> 00:25:27,340
 Left to Rome for his execution.

641
00:25:27,340 --> 00:25:28,500
 And as he was being transported,

642
00:25:28,500 --> 00:25:30,880
 Polycarp was commanded to renounce Christ.

643
00:25:30,880 --> 00:25:33,600
 To which he responded, I can't.

644
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:40,340
 86 years I have served him and he has done me no wrong.

645
00:25:40,340 --> 00:25:42,960
 How can I blaspheme my king who saved me?

646
00:25:44,380 --> 00:25:48,180
 The governor of Rome warned him,

647
00:25:48,180 --> 00:25:50,860
 Polycarp, I have wild beasts.

648
00:25:50,860 --> 00:25:52,200
 I will throw you to them.

649
00:25:52,200 --> 00:25:55,420
 Polycarp simply said, call for them.

650
00:25:55,420 --> 00:25:58,980
 When he was threatened to be burned alive,

651
00:25:58,980 --> 00:26:02,900
 Polycarp answered that judgment by fire is temporary,

652
00:26:02,900 --> 00:26:05,680
 while judgment by God is eternal.

653
00:26:05,680 --> 00:26:11,120
 After realizing that Polycarp was not going to surrender,

654
00:26:11,120 --> 00:26:14,420
 the governor of Rome ordered that Polycarp be burned alive.

655
00:26:14,420 --> 00:26:16,700
 As they were going to tie him,

656
00:26:16,700 --> 00:26:18,780
 Polycarp said there was no need,

657
00:26:18,780 --> 00:26:20,820
 for he would stand in the will of God for his life,

658
00:26:20,820 --> 00:26:23,500
 even if it meant he had to stand within the fire.

659
00:26:23,500 --> 00:26:26,740
 And yet history records something amazing in this moment,

660
00:26:26,740 --> 00:26:30,420
 that as they lit the pyre and the flames arose,

661
00:26:30,420 --> 00:26:33,580
 they bent around Polycarp like the wind

662
00:26:33,580 --> 00:26:35,700
 feeling a ship's sails.

663
00:26:35,700 --> 00:26:38,700
 The flames did not touch him.

664
00:26:38,700 --> 00:26:40,380
 There was divine protection on his life.

665
00:26:40,380 --> 00:26:43,900
 So far to the point that the soldiers knew

666
00:26:43,900 --> 00:26:44,980
 we'll have to kill them ourselves.

667
00:26:44,980 --> 00:26:48,260
 And so they stabbed him in the side,

668
00:26:48,260 --> 00:26:51,860
 in the same position where Christ, his Christ was crucified.

669
00:26:51,860 --> 00:26:55,900
 This is what courage looks like, guys.

670
00:26:55,900 --> 00:26:58,980
 This is what it looks like when great men do great things,

671
00:26:58,980 --> 00:27:00,460
 compelled by conviction.

672
00:27:00,460 --> 00:27:02,860
 And gentlemen, we got to find some,

673
00:27:02,860 --> 00:27:05,180
 because courage is not the absence of fear.

674
00:27:05,180 --> 00:27:06,900
 It is the conquering of it.

675
00:27:06,900 --> 00:27:08,520
 And so the question cannot be,

676
00:27:08,520 --> 00:27:10,340
 are you willing to die for your convictions?

677
00:27:10,340 --> 00:27:12,300
 Instead, the question must be instead,

678
00:27:12,300 --> 00:27:14,700
 are you willing to live for them?

679
00:27:14,700 --> 00:27:16,460
 Because here's the truth, in our world,

680
00:27:16,460 --> 00:27:18,100
 you may not be killed for your convictions,

681
00:27:18,100 --> 00:27:20,620
 but they will certainly cost you.

682
00:27:20,620 --> 00:27:23,100
 And so you need to make a decision today

683
00:27:23,100 --> 00:27:25,540
 what you actually will stand for.

684
00:27:25,540 --> 00:27:26,620
 You need to make a decision.

685
00:27:26,620 --> 00:27:28,500
 Like you must decide, are you going,

686
00:27:28,500 --> 00:27:29,940
 what kind of man are you going to be

687
00:27:29,940 --> 00:27:31,800
 when nobody is around to see it?

688
00:27:31,800 --> 00:27:32,980
 You need to make a decision.

689
00:27:32,980 --> 00:27:35,580
 What kind of husband will you be whenever you do?

690
00:27:35,580 --> 00:27:37,980
 Place your vows, say your I do's,

691
00:27:37,980 --> 00:27:39,340
 and are wedded to your bride.

692
00:27:39,340 --> 00:27:40,580
 You need to make a decision.

693
00:27:40,580 --> 00:27:41,940
 What kind of father will you be

694
00:27:41,940 --> 00:27:43,340
 when you have a little girl, a little boy,

695
00:27:43,340 --> 00:27:45,940
 looking up to you and catching influence

696
00:27:45,940 --> 00:27:47,540
 as you walk with Jesus?

697
00:27:47,540 --> 00:27:48,620
 You need to make a decision.

698
00:27:48,620 --> 00:27:49,700
 What kind of boss will you be

699
00:27:49,700 --> 00:27:51,500
 when people, subordinates beneath you,

700
00:27:51,500 --> 00:27:54,100
 are actually looking to you and depending on you for guidance?

701
00:27:54,100 --> 00:27:55,020
 You need to make a decision.

702
00:27:55,020 --> 00:27:56,940
 What kind of a neighbor are you going to be

703
00:27:56,940 --> 00:28:00,060
 whenever those neighbors are extremely inconvenient

704
00:28:00,060 --> 00:28:01,380
 and you need to make a decision.

705
00:28:01,380 --> 00:28:03,780
 What kind of believer will I be

706
00:28:03,780 --> 00:28:08,660
 whenever my God calls me because he most certainly will?

707
00:28:08,660 --> 00:28:11,820
 Will I rise up in faith, stand on my convictions,

708
00:28:11,820 --> 00:28:13,900
 or will I bow down whenever Haman,

709
00:28:13,900 --> 00:28:16,860
 the Hamans of this world, ask me to do so?

710
00:28:16,860 --> 00:28:17,860
 No, you be like Mordecai.

711
00:28:17,860 --> 00:28:19,780
 You know where your convictions are

712
00:28:19,780 --> 00:28:21,540
 so that way when the call to bow comes,

713
00:28:21,540 --> 00:28:24,300
 you are already standing and you have great confidence

714
00:28:24,300 --> 00:28:26,600
 that you're right where you're supposed to be.

715
00:28:26,600 --> 00:28:29,260
 You need conviction, gentlemen.

716
00:28:29,260 --> 00:28:32,780
 When your convictions are settled,

717
00:28:32,780 --> 00:28:34,380
 courage becomes possible.

718
00:28:36,120 --> 00:28:38,820
 And so settle your convictions here tonight.

719
00:28:38,820 --> 00:28:41,700
 Now, for you ladies, I've already said it.

720
00:28:41,700 --> 00:28:44,260
 Conviction absolutely leads to courage.

721
00:28:44,260 --> 00:28:46,220
 Again, nothing we're talking about

722
00:28:46,220 --> 00:28:48,980
 is exclusive to one gender or the other here.

723
00:28:48,980 --> 00:28:50,940
 And yet, what we see by way of Esther

724
00:28:50,940 --> 00:28:54,020
 is an orientation that's a little bit different.

725
00:28:54,020 --> 00:28:58,540
 We read this in chapter four, verses 13 through 17,

726
00:28:58,540 --> 00:29:00,220
 as she's responding to the fact

727
00:29:00,220 --> 00:29:03,140
 that Haman and the king have cooked up this decree

728
00:29:03,140 --> 00:29:05,040
 that all Jews should be killed.

729
00:29:06,460 --> 00:29:07,700
 And Mordecai is pleading with her,

730
00:29:07,700 --> 00:29:08,780
 "Hey, you gotta do something."

731
00:29:08,780 --> 00:29:09,600
 This is what it says.

732
00:29:09,600 --> 00:29:12,100
 "Then Mordecai told them to reply to Esther,

733
00:29:12,100 --> 00:29:14,220
 "Do not think to yourself that in the king's palace

734
00:29:14,220 --> 00:29:16,220
 "you'll escape any more than all the other Jews.

735
00:29:16,220 --> 00:29:17,660
 "For if you keep silent at this time,

736
00:29:17,660 --> 00:29:20,180
 "relief and deliverance will rise for the Jews

737
00:29:20,180 --> 00:29:21,480
 "from another place,

738
00:29:21,480 --> 00:29:24,100
 "but you and your father's house, you'll perish.

739
00:29:24,100 --> 00:29:26,540
 "And who knows whether you have not come to the kingdom

740
00:29:26,540 --> 00:29:28,700
 "for such a time as this.

741
00:29:28,700 --> 00:29:30,700
 "And then Esther told them to reply to Mordecai,

742
00:29:30,700 --> 00:29:35,100
 "Go, gather all the Jews to be found in Susa

743
00:29:35,100 --> 00:29:36,740
 "and hold a fast on my behalf

744
00:29:36,740 --> 00:29:40,400
 "and do not eat or drink for three days, night or day.

745
00:29:40,400 --> 00:29:43,060
 "I and my young women will also fast as you do,

746
00:29:43,060 --> 00:29:44,460
 "then I will go to the king.

747
00:29:44,460 --> 00:29:50,260
 "Though it is against the law and if I perish, I perish."

748
00:29:50,260 --> 00:29:51,300
 Mordecai then went away

749
00:29:51,300 --> 00:29:53,780
 and he did everything that Esther had ordered him.

750
00:29:53,780 --> 00:29:56,100
 You see, Esther shows us that for godly women,

751
00:29:56,100 --> 00:29:58,600
 courage comes from compassion.

752
00:29:58,600 --> 00:30:00,580
 Courage comes from compassion.

753
00:30:00,580 --> 00:30:02,460
 Esther's courage is not a generic kind of courage.

754
00:30:02,460 --> 00:30:04,020
 It's a very specific kind of courage

755
00:30:04,020 --> 00:30:06,140
 that is in response to the needs of her people,

756
00:30:06,140 --> 00:30:09,020
 which makes sense when you consider that women,

757
00:30:09,020 --> 00:30:11,580
 by design, have an orientation towards nurturing.

758
00:30:11,580 --> 00:30:12,740
 It's amazing.

759
00:30:12,740 --> 00:30:16,700
 Now, I've had some direct exposure to this,

760
00:30:16,700 --> 00:30:19,840
 but to see what mothers will do for their children.

761
00:30:19,840 --> 00:30:22,100
 It's an incredible kind of strength.

762
00:30:22,100 --> 00:30:25,540
 They will carry a child for nine months in their womb

763
00:30:25,540 --> 00:30:27,540
 and it takes an especial kind of strength

764
00:30:27,540 --> 00:30:30,140
 to forego sushi over the course of those nine months.

765
00:30:30,140 --> 00:30:32,020
 Like, that's an incredible cost.

766
00:30:32,020 --> 00:30:33,860
 My wife is living with right now.

767
00:30:33,860 --> 00:30:36,900
 You see that they go through labor and delivery

768
00:30:36,900 --> 00:30:37,860
 and I've never been in that position.

769
00:30:37,860 --> 00:30:39,020
 I don't wanna be in that position

770
00:30:39,020 --> 00:30:40,580
 because it looks very difficult

771
00:30:40,580 --> 00:30:42,860
 and yet mothers, they choose to go back

772
00:30:42,860 --> 00:30:44,440
 again and again and again because of the joy

773
00:30:44,440 --> 00:30:48,820
 of having children by way of God's own hand.

774
00:30:48,820 --> 00:30:51,220
 They wake up all hours of the night.

775
00:30:51,220 --> 00:30:53,300
 If ever the baby cries, they will change diaper

776
00:30:53,300 --> 00:30:55,220
 after diaper, after diaper, after diaper

777
00:30:55,220 --> 00:30:56,740
 with no sort of acknowledgement

778
00:30:56,740 --> 00:30:58,940
 or appreciation by the baby whatsoever.

779
00:30:58,940 --> 00:31:00,900
 I would love for the guy to just like give me a wink,

780
00:31:00,900 --> 00:31:02,340
 you know, like, "Hey man, you're doing good.

781
00:31:02,340 --> 00:31:03,180
 "Thanks for doing this."

782
00:31:03,180 --> 00:31:05,980
 I don't know, one day I'll probably do it for you.

783
00:31:05,980 --> 00:31:09,500
 They all know that at the end of the day,

784
00:31:09,500 --> 00:31:14,500
 their strength is needed for those that are compelled.

785
00:31:14,500 --> 00:31:17,460
 Their strength is needed for those

786
00:31:17,460 --> 00:31:19,740
 that have compelled their love within

787
00:31:19,740 --> 00:31:23,380
 and it's the reason compassion is such a strong motivator

788
00:31:23,380 --> 00:31:24,860
 and yet it's not exclusive to women.

789
00:31:24,860 --> 00:31:25,900
 Look at Jesus.

790
00:31:25,900 --> 00:31:28,820
 This was his motivation in Luke 13, verse 34.

791
00:31:28,820 --> 00:31:31,540
 Jerusalem, Jerusalem, you who kill the prophets

792
00:31:31,540 --> 00:31:32,500
 and stone those who sin to you,

793
00:31:32,500 --> 00:31:35,220
 how often have I longed to gather your children together

794
00:31:35,220 --> 00:31:38,180
 as a hen gathers her chicks under her wings.

795
00:31:38,180 --> 00:31:40,420
 There's a maternal quality to this

796
00:31:40,420 --> 00:31:41,860
 and yet you were not willing.

797
00:31:41,860 --> 00:31:45,780
 What I love about Esther's example in this moment

798
00:31:45,780 --> 00:31:48,860
 as she responds to the news that like every Jew

799
00:31:48,860 --> 00:31:50,140
 will be destroyed and Mordecai's like,

800
00:31:50,140 --> 00:31:51,540
 "We gotta do something."

801
00:31:51,540 --> 00:31:54,260
 She does not just spring into action.

802
00:31:54,260 --> 00:31:55,780
 She doesn't act impulsively.

803
00:31:55,780 --> 00:31:57,300
 It's probably why God chose a woman

804
00:31:57,300 --> 00:31:59,020
 for this specific task instead of a man.

805
00:31:59,020 --> 00:32:00,620
 Like a guy would hop in and just be like,

806
00:32:00,620 --> 00:32:01,660
 "Ready, fire, aim."

807
00:32:01,660 --> 00:32:03,140
 And that's a really bad decision

808
00:32:03,140 --> 00:32:05,100
 because this is a very complicated situation.

809
00:32:05,100 --> 00:32:07,220
 He wants to work through a woman

810
00:32:07,220 --> 00:32:10,420
 that can think very clearly, which is what she does.

811
00:32:10,420 --> 00:32:12,340
 She thinks clearly under pressure.

812
00:32:12,340 --> 00:32:13,660
 She sends for answers.

813
00:32:13,660 --> 00:32:14,740
 She considers the cost.

814
00:32:14,740 --> 00:32:16,500
 And then she makes the hardest statement

815
00:32:16,500 --> 00:32:18,780
 any woman has ever made in the Bible.

816
00:32:18,780 --> 00:32:21,460
 If I perish, I perish.

817
00:32:21,460 --> 00:32:23,780
 That's a different kind of woman.

818
00:32:23,780 --> 00:32:26,140
 When everybody else would have talked themselves out of it,

819
00:32:26,140 --> 00:32:28,580
 Esther talked herself into it

820
00:32:28,580 --> 00:32:30,580
 because that's what godly women do.

821
00:32:30,580 --> 00:32:32,380
 That's courage, ladies.

822
00:32:32,380 --> 00:32:35,100
 Is there something that you have talked yourself out of

823
00:32:35,100 --> 00:32:37,540
 that God is trying to talk you into here tonight?

824
00:32:37,540 --> 00:32:40,380
 That he's compelling you to consider?

825
00:32:40,380 --> 00:32:43,500
 Like maybe you've talked yourself out of forgiving someone

826
00:32:43,500 --> 00:32:45,620
 because that's just gonna be way too difficult

827
00:32:45,620 --> 00:32:47,060
 and it's gonna open up old wounds.

828
00:32:47,060 --> 00:32:49,060
 Maybe you've talked yourself out of a difficult conversation

829
00:32:49,060 --> 00:32:50,580
 where you're actually the guilty party

830
00:32:50,580 --> 00:32:52,260
 and you're gonna have to swallow your pride

831
00:32:52,260 --> 00:32:53,380
 and take responsibility.

832
00:32:53,380 --> 00:32:54,940
 Maybe you've talked yourself out of serving

833
00:32:54,940 --> 00:32:57,220
 because you're not sure that what you have to offer

834
00:32:57,220 --> 00:32:59,740
 is enough for everything that people are going to need.

835
00:32:59,740 --> 00:33:01,700
 Maybe you have talked yourself out of ending

836
00:33:01,700 --> 00:33:03,460
 that relationship even though you know

837
00:33:03,460 --> 00:33:04,860
 it's just not honoring God.

838
00:33:04,860 --> 00:33:07,140
 Maybe you've talked yourself out of taking a step of faith.

839
00:33:07,140 --> 00:33:09,500
 When's the last time you took a step of faith?

840
00:33:09,500 --> 00:33:12,460
 Men and women in the room, both.

841
00:33:12,460 --> 00:33:14,420
 The last time you took a step of faith?

842
00:33:14,420 --> 00:33:17,420
 To join a church?

843
00:33:17,420 --> 00:33:18,860
 To get baptized?

844
00:33:18,860 --> 00:33:19,700
 Come to awaken?

845
00:33:19,700 --> 00:33:20,900
 I don't know.

846
00:33:20,900 --> 00:33:21,820
 Share your faith?

847
00:33:21,820 --> 00:33:25,500
 When was the last time you took a step of faith?

848
00:33:25,500 --> 00:33:28,340
 Maybe God is saying, ladies, I want you to do that

849
00:33:28,340 --> 00:33:30,100
 even if it costs you.

850
00:33:30,100 --> 00:33:32,620
 Because here's the thing about courage.

851
00:33:32,620 --> 00:33:34,940
 Courage does not mean you stop counting the cost.

852
00:33:34,940 --> 00:33:36,500
 What it does mean is that you realize

853
00:33:36,500 --> 00:33:38,580
 someone else is worth the price.

854
00:33:38,580 --> 00:33:43,420
 So who needs you to be brave?

855
00:33:43,420 --> 00:33:45,220
 Like in your life, ladies, here tonight,

856
00:33:45,220 --> 00:33:48,220
 as you know, courage is compelled by compassion.

857
00:33:48,220 --> 00:33:50,300
 Who needs you in your world to be brave?

858
00:33:50,300 --> 00:33:51,500
 Is it a friend?

859
00:33:51,500 --> 00:33:52,580
 Is it a sibling?

860
00:33:52,580 --> 00:33:55,580
 Is it a coworker that needs you

861
00:33:55,580 --> 00:33:57,460
 to take an invested interest in who they are?

862
00:33:57,460 --> 00:33:58,860
 Is it a family member that needs you

863
00:33:58,860 --> 00:34:00,660
 to actually share the gospel with them?

864
00:34:00,660 --> 00:34:02,180
 What is it that someone is needing of you

865
00:34:02,180 --> 00:34:03,820
 that will require your bravery?

866
00:34:03,820 --> 00:34:06,220
 Jesus knew that we needed Him to be brave.

867
00:34:06,220 --> 00:34:08,540
 And the beauty of this is, as is true to every point,

868
00:34:08,540 --> 00:34:10,380
 He is brave in both regards.

869
00:34:10,380 --> 00:34:13,020
 He is brave with conviction, doing all that God asks Him,

870
00:34:13,020 --> 00:34:14,100
 and He is brave with compassion,

871
00:34:14,100 --> 00:34:16,540
 moving towards those whom He loves.

872
00:34:16,540 --> 00:34:18,460
 He is the perfect embodiment of this

873
00:34:18,460 --> 00:34:21,460
 because Jesus has the same courage we're called to have.

874
00:34:21,460 --> 00:34:22,780
 You cannot do this on your own.

875
00:34:22,780 --> 00:34:24,500
 You must do it by Him, but praise God,

876
00:34:24,500 --> 00:34:26,060
 He has already done it for you.

877
00:34:27,500 --> 00:34:30,060
 The third way that we see how men and women relate

878
00:34:30,060 --> 00:34:33,980
 is through different perspectives, but the same wisdom.

879
00:34:33,980 --> 00:34:36,620
 Different perspectives, but the same wisdom.

880
00:34:36,620 --> 00:34:37,700
 I won't spend a lot of time on this one

881
00:34:37,700 --> 00:34:39,100
 'cause we've already been talking about this a little bit,

882
00:34:39,100 --> 00:34:41,020
 but I do think it's helpful for us to understand

883
00:34:41,020 --> 00:34:42,620
 that Mordecai and Esther,

884
00:34:42,620 --> 00:34:44,940
 they process their situation very differently.

885
00:34:44,940 --> 00:34:46,260
 And that tells us something about the way

886
00:34:46,260 --> 00:34:48,700
 that men and women are supposed to partner together

887
00:34:48,700 --> 00:34:50,420
 in solving great problems

888
00:34:50,420 --> 00:34:52,300
 or navigating difficult situations.

889
00:34:52,300 --> 00:34:54,820
 You see, Mordecai, he springs into action.

890
00:34:54,820 --> 00:34:55,980
 He's ready to go.

891
00:34:55,980 --> 00:34:57,620
 He is an action orientation,

892
00:34:57,620 --> 00:34:59,980
 which is traditionally pretty true of men.

893
00:34:59,980 --> 00:35:01,420
 And yet what you see in Esther

894
00:35:01,420 --> 00:35:03,060
 is she takes stock of the situation.

895
00:35:03,060 --> 00:35:04,700
 She considers what's going on.

896
00:35:04,700 --> 00:35:07,740
 She acquires more information.

897
00:35:07,740 --> 00:35:09,980
 And that's good news

898
00:35:09,980 --> 00:35:12,300
 because those two things complement each other very well

899
00:35:12,300 --> 00:35:14,100
 and will serve one another in the end.

900
00:35:14,100 --> 00:35:16,380
 So for men, you gotta know that you're,

901
00:35:16,380 --> 00:35:19,700
 according to Mordecai, someone who will quickly initiate.

902
00:35:19,700 --> 00:35:20,860
 That's part of who you are.

903
00:35:20,860 --> 00:35:21,980
 You will quickly initiate.

904
00:35:21,980 --> 00:35:23,220
 That was Mordecai's response.

905
00:35:23,220 --> 00:35:24,460
 He heard the decree.

906
00:35:24,460 --> 00:35:25,660
 He mourned publicly.

907
00:35:25,660 --> 00:35:28,780
 He calls up Esther and he presses her to act.

908
00:35:28,780 --> 00:35:29,820
 Why?

909
00:35:29,820 --> 00:35:32,500
 Because he knows something needs to be done,

910
00:35:32,500 --> 00:35:35,420
 and yet he realizes, "I can't do it."

911
00:35:35,420 --> 00:35:37,540
 He knows that he is out of his depth.

912
00:35:37,540 --> 00:35:39,860
 He does not have the kind of access that she does.

913
00:35:39,860 --> 00:35:41,500
 And so he calls her up and says,

914
00:35:41,500 --> 00:35:43,540
 "Hey, you've gotta do something about this."

915
00:35:43,540 --> 00:35:45,020
 You see, this is important for men.

916
00:35:45,020 --> 00:35:47,260
 You can't solve every problem on your own.

917
00:35:47,260 --> 00:35:51,140
 It's not possible.

918
00:35:52,100 --> 00:35:56,740
 And yet godly men, they acknowledge their limitations

919
00:35:56,740 --> 00:35:59,980
 and they acknowledge them quickly.

920
00:35:59,980 --> 00:36:00,820
 I love it.

921
00:36:00,820 --> 00:36:03,340
 Like he doesn't plan things out for her.

922
00:36:03,340 --> 00:36:06,020
 He doesn't micromanage her progress.

923
00:36:06,020 --> 00:36:07,500
 He doesn't assume that she can't do it.

924
00:36:07,500 --> 00:36:09,460
 He literally comes to her and he's like,

925
00:36:09,460 --> 00:36:12,060
 "Hey, this is really bad.

926
00:36:12,060 --> 00:36:15,260
 "And I think that God's put you in a position

927
00:36:15,260 --> 00:36:16,680
 "to do something about it.

928
00:36:16,680 --> 00:36:18,340
 "What do you think?"

929
00:36:18,340 --> 00:36:20,660
 I remember having a similar conversation in my own life.

930
00:36:20,660 --> 00:36:22,220
 I was living in Houston and we were riding back

931
00:36:22,220 --> 00:36:23,420
 from a retreat.

932
00:36:23,420 --> 00:36:25,900
 And as I was visiting with a girl in the car,

933
00:36:25,900 --> 00:36:28,500
 this girl who, she was upper management

934
00:36:28,500 --> 00:36:30,020
 at a big time construction company,

935
00:36:30,020 --> 00:36:31,660
 making way more money than I was.

936
00:36:31,660 --> 00:36:35,380
 I just knew by way of my observation of her that weekend

937
00:36:35,380 --> 00:36:38,180
 that God had just like uniquely put something in her

938
00:36:38,180 --> 00:36:41,100
 that could speak to women that were struggling

939
00:36:41,100 --> 00:36:43,300
 in their singleness, that had been single longer

940
00:36:43,300 --> 00:36:44,140
 than they wanted.

941
00:36:44,140 --> 00:36:44,980
 And so I just looked at her and I was like,

942
00:36:44,980 --> 00:36:48,580
 "Hey, Megan, I just think that God has given you

943
00:36:48,580 --> 00:36:51,860
 "a unique voice to people that have struggled

944
00:36:51,860 --> 00:36:54,780
 "with something that they didn't have planned

945
00:36:54,780 --> 00:36:57,580
 "for their lives, that you yourself

946
00:36:57,580 --> 00:36:58,800
 "have dealt with personally.

947
00:36:58,800 --> 00:37:01,120
 "And yet you have navigated so very beautifully.

948
00:37:01,120 --> 00:37:03,860
 "I think he has called you to do something about that."

949
00:37:03,860 --> 00:37:09,580
 And the amazing thing is, is she ended up leaving that job

950
00:37:09,580 --> 00:37:13,980
 and accepting a position on my team

951
00:37:13,980 --> 00:37:18,100
 and moving towards this very specific stewardship

952
00:37:18,100 --> 00:37:18,940
 that God had given her,

953
00:37:18,940 --> 00:37:20,980
 which she was meant to take action on.

954
00:37:20,980 --> 00:37:24,900
 Guys, we gotta do stuff like this.

955
00:37:24,900 --> 00:37:28,340
 We need to recognize how God has uniquely gifted our sisters

956
00:37:28,340 --> 00:37:30,820
 and we need to honor them by calling them to action

957
00:37:30,820 --> 00:37:32,660
 where they can make a difference.

958
00:37:32,660 --> 00:37:34,380
 We don't need to be threatened by them.

959
00:37:34,380 --> 00:37:36,320
 And what I've seen as I've observed men

960
00:37:36,320 --> 00:37:38,900
 is that in an effort to be a really good leader,

961
00:37:38,900 --> 00:37:43,360
 we often diminish the agency of our sisters.

962
00:37:43,360 --> 00:37:47,100
 So ask their opinions, seek their involvement,

963
00:37:47,100 --> 00:37:49,580
 listen to what they have to say,

964
00:37:49,580 --> 00:37:52,340
 and even follow their lead if the situation says so.

965
00:37:52,340 --> 00:37:54,740
 That's what Mordecai does.

966
00:37:54,740 --> 00:37:58,200
 In Esther 4, verse 17, Mordecai then went away

967
00:37:58,200 --> 00:38:00,700
 and he did everything as Esther had ordered him.

968
00:38:00,700 --> 00:38:03,780
 He didn't walk away mumbling,

969
00:38:03,780 --> 00:38:04,620
 "Who does she think she is?

970
00:38:04,620 --> 00:38:05,620
 "Like, she's not the boss of me.

971
00:38:05,620 --> 00:38:07,100
 "How dare she tell me what I'm supposed to do?"

972
00:38:07,100 --> 00:38:08,540
 He doesn't do that.

973
00:38:08,540 --> 00:38:10,660
 Instead, he acknowledges the fact

974
00:38:10,660 --> 00:38:13,520
 that she is in a position to make a greater impact

975
00:38:13,520 --> 00:38:15,700
 in this moment than I am.

976
00:38:15,700 --> 00:38:19,040
 And so he respects that fact, acknowledges his limitations,

977
00:38:19,040 --> 00:38:20,580
 and then moves in response.

978
00:38:20,580 --> 00:38:21,780
 That's wisdom.

979
00:38:21,780 --> 00:38:23,860
 Now, where godly men quickly initiate,

980
00:38:23,860 --> 00:38:26,220
 what we see from Esther is that godly women

981
00:38:26,220 --> 00:38:30,180
 shrewdly consider, shrewdly consider.

982
00:38:30,180 --> 00:38:33,060
 Like Esther hears that there's bad news.

983
00:38:33,060 --> 00:38:34,300
 All the Jews are gonna be destroyed.

984
00:38:34,300 --> 00:38:35,220
 And yet what she doesn't do

985
00:38:35,220 --> 00:38:37,500
 is she doesn't like march into the throne room,

986
00:38:37,500 --> 00:38:39,340
 all boss girl energy and look at the king

987
00:38:39,340 --> 00:38:41,700
 and tell him how dare he do this to his people.

988
00:38:41,700 --> 00:38:42,700
 She doesn't operate like that.

989
00:38:42,700 --> 00:38:45,820
 Instead, she calls for a fast.

990
00:38:45,820 --> 00:38:47,540
 She prepares her approach.

991
00:38:47,540 --> 00:38:49,100
 She comes to the king in chapter five

992
00:38:49,100 --> 00:38:50,820
 with wisdom and with timing.

993
00:38:50,820 --> 00:38:52,540
 And by the end of chapter six, she has hosted

994
00:38:52,540 --> 00:38:55,860
 not one, but two banquets with the king

995
00:38:55,860 --> 00:38:59,740
 before ever mentioning a word to him of her request.

996
00:38:59,740 --> 00:39:02,020
 That is shrewdness.

997
00:39:02,020 --> 00:39:03,580
 She is perceptive of the situation.

998
00:39:03,580 --> 00:39:06,100
 She is calculated in her decisions.

999
00:39:06,100 --> 00:39:08,220
 She is humble in her words,

1000
00:39:08,220 --> 00:39:09,980
 and she surrendered to God's will.

1001
00:39:10,980 --> 00:39:14,780
 Put in one word, Esther is wise in this moment.

1002
00:39:14,780 --> 00:39:18,540
 She understands the situational dynamics of the moment

1003
00:39:18,540 --> 00:39:23,420
 and she maneuvers them so very carefully.

1004
00:39:23,420 --> 00:39:24,620
 I love this.

1005
00:39:24,620 --> 00:39:29,620
 Her success in the moment requires her femininity.

1006
00:39:29,620 --> 00:39:33,580
 She need not discard that

1007
00:39:33,580 --> 00:39:35,660
 which God has uniquely imbued her with.

1008
00:39:35,660 --> 00:39:37,060
 She embraces it.

1009
00:39:37,060 --> 00:39:39,900
 And as she does so, she can think through the situation

1010
00:39:39,900 --> 00:39:42,740
 in a way a man might more than likely never could.

1011
00:39:42,740 --> 00:39:44,700
 This situation required a woman's touch.

1012
00:39:44,700 --> 00:39:46,300
 And that's what she had.

1013
00:39:46,300 --> 00:39:48,100
 That's what she could give.

1014
00:39:48,100 --> 00:39:50,700
 Ladies, this is very simple.

1015
00:39:50,700 --> 00:39:52,460
 We need you to be you.

1016
00:39:52,460 --> 00:39:55,100
 We need you to think like a woman

1017
00:39:55,100 --> 00:39:56,900
 and talk like a woman and act like a woman

1018
00:39:56,900 --> 00:39:58,820
 and process like a woman and strategize like a woman

1019
00:39:58,820 --> 00:40:00,220
 and problem solve like a woman

1020
00:40:00,220 --> 00:40:02,940
 because not a man in here can do that.

1021
00:40:02,940 --> 00:40:06,220
 We need you to be you.

1022
00:40:06,220 --> 00:40:09,300
 Mordecai's instinct to act was needed.

1023
00:40:09,300 --> 00:40:11,540
 Esther's instinct to consider was needed.

1024
00:40:11,540 --> 00:40:14,820
 And God is saying the same to all of us.

1025
00:40:14,820 --> 00:40:15,900
 So men, listen to me.

1026
00:40:15,900 --> 00:40:20,900
 The wisest thing you can do is ask her what she thinks.

1027
00:40:20,900 --> 00:40:26,380
 Ladies, sometimes the wisest thing you can do

1028
00:40:26,380 --> 00:40:29,580
 is trust him when he says, "We gotta move."

1029
00:40:29,580 --> 00:40:31,620
 Because as we give each other the benefit of the doubt

1030
00:40:31,620 --> 00:40:33,220
 and we don't play the blame game,

1031
00:40:33,220 --> 00:40:36,220
 we end up moving and solving

1032
00:40:36,220 --> 00:40:39,780
 and ultimately accomplishing all that God has meant

1033
00:40:39,780 --> 00:40:42,340
 for us to do by way of our partnership.

1034
00:40:42,340 --> 00:40:46,100
 That's what happens in this story.

1035
00:40:46,100 --> 00:40:48,940
 Esther exposes Haman's treachery to the king.

1036
00:40:48,940 --> 00:40:51,020
 The king has Haman killed.

1037
00:40:51,020 --> 00:40:52,660
 In a stunning turn of events,

1038
00:40:52,660 --> 00:40:55,580
 Haman is replaced by Mordecai, his arch enemy,

1039
00:40:55,580 --> 00:40:56,900
 as Persia's new CFO.

1040
00:40:56,900 --> 00:40:59,140
 And together, Mordecai and Esther, they save the Jews.

1041
00:40:59,140 --> 00:41:00,700
 Hallelujah.

1042
00:41:00,700 --> 00:41:02,020
 How do they do all of it?

1043
00:41:02,020 --> 00:41:05,300
 Because, and this is your last point,

1044
00:41:05,300 --> 00:41:06,460
 they have different contributions,

1045
00:41:06,460 --> 00:41:08,180
 but they have the same goal.

